## Container image

```bash
docker build --build-context contracts=../{{ .contracts }} -t {{ .appId }} .
```

Multi-stage build on the .NET 10 chiseled runtime. The shared contracts
sibling enters the build as the `contracts` named context (it lies outside
this build context). The image contains only the app — the Dapr sidecar and
components come from the deployment environment.

## Pipeline

One sweep per run (`src/Sweep.cs`, hosted by the framework's
`RunToCompletionRunner`, which owns the sidecar lifecycle, tracing, and the
0/1/2 exit-code mapping via `src/StreamJob.cs`):

```text
// Sweep transitions (per file):
//
//         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
//         │ 1. List incoming/           ├──── empty ─► quiet exit 0
//         └──────────────┬──────────────┘
//                        ▼
//         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
//         │ 2. Streamed extraction      │  matched to a streamed extractor
//         └──────────────┬──────────────┘  by entity type; constant-memory
//                        │                │  validate+transform → JSONL output
//                        ▼
//         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
//         │ 3. ReferencePublishStep     │  one claim-check CloudEvent
//         └──────────────┬──────────────┘  (subject = source file name)
//                        ▼
//         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
//         │ 4. Dapr topic publisher     │
//         └──────────────┬──────────────┘
//                        ▼
//         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
//         │ 5. Archive input            │  incoming/ → processed/
//         └─────────────────────────────┘
//
// Unknown entity / streamed failure routes a business incident and leaves
// the file; a zero-valid file is archived without an event; a technical
// failure leaves the file for the next run.
```
{{- if .empty }}

The entity mapping, deserializer, process step, and reference construction
throw `NotImplementedException` — this project was scaffolded with empty
bodies for a migration agent to fill in. The sweep wiring (extraction,
publish, archive, business-incident routing) is already in place; define the
producer's file→entity rule in `Sweep.EntityTypeFor`, the record-array path
in `src/Process/Streamed/Deserializer.cs`, the validate+transform in
`{{ .contract }}ProcessStep`, and the reference shape in
`src/Process/ReferencePublishStep.cs`.

The sweep-run tests fail from the start by design (the throwing steps route
the run to a failure without publishing). The suite flips green piece by
piece as the steps are implemented — the failing tests are the to-do list.
{{- else }}

1. The sweep lists the files directly under the incoming prefix.
2. Each file is matched to its registered streamed extractor by entity type
   and streamed (constant memory) to the output prefix as JSONL.
3. `ReferencePublishStep` builds the one claim-check CloudEvent from the
   streamed counts; subject = source file name.
4. The Dapr topic publisher sends it to `pubsub` / `{{ .topic }}`.
5. The consumed input moves to the processed prefix — which is also what
   hides it from the next sweep.
{{- end }}
